  "folderSentToInbox": "{n} sent to the inbox this session.",
  "helpInboxTitle": "Review inbox",
  "helpInboxBody": "Every proof of payment that arrives (WhatsApp, email, upload link, “Share with COROC”, folder or in-app upload) is read automatically: amount, date, payer, recipient, reference and bank, each with its confidence. COROC identifies the client by number, email, link or folder, checks the payment went to your accounts, that the date makes sense and that it is not a duplicate (same reference, amount and date, or the same file), and records the payment on its own only when everything is unambiguous. The rest stays in the inbox: on the left the file with what was read highlighted, on the right the data to correct, the client and loan, and the balance before and after. Approve with Enter; you can also reject with a reason or mark “Not a proof of payment”. An automatic record can be reverted with one tap during the configured window; after that, with a formal reversal.",
  "helpUploadLinkTitle": "Borrower upload link",
  "helpUploadLinkBody": "Each loan can have a personal link. The borrower opens it in any browser, in their language and without installing anything: they see their balance, next installment and payment plan, and upload the photo or PDF of the proof. Because the link identifies the borrower, the payment goes to the right loan. Create, copy or share it from the loan summary; “Change link” invalidates the previous one immediately and “Deactivate” turns it off.",
  "helpShareTitle": "Share with COROC",
  "helpShareBody": "On Android and iOS, COROC appears when you share or open an image or PDF: in WhatsApp, tap the proof, “Share” and COROC. The file goes to the inbox; since the phone does not say who sent it, COROC suggests the most likely client (by payer name and amount) and you confirm with one tap. On desktop, drop the file in the _Inbox folder or in the client folder, or use “Upload proof of payment”.",
  "helpReceivingTitle": "Receiving accounts and automatic recording",
  "helpReceivingBody": "In Settings, register the accounts where you get paid (holder, bank and last 4 digits). The recipient on each proof is compared with them ignoring accents; if it does not match, the payment is never recorded automatically. Also choose the mode: “Automatic with audit” records unambiguous payments instantly and lets you revert them within a window; “Prior approval” sends everything to the inbox. The minimum confidence, maximum age of the proof and revert window are set there too.",
