  "whatsappActivateCloud": "Turn on automatic mode",
  "helpMessagingTitle": "Automatic messages and assisted mode",
  "helpMessagingBody": "COROC sends six automatic messages: welcome with the payment plan, installment reminder (1 day before and on the due date), payment received with its receipt, installment past due (1 day after), monthly statement and payoff letter. Each one is turned on separately and has its template in every language under Messages › Templates.\n\nIn assisted mode COROC writes each message and leaves it in “To send today”: when you tap “Send on WhatsApp” the rules are checked again and WhatsApp opens with the text ready; you just tap “Send”. Receipts include a secure download link (30 days) and, on a phone, you can share the PDF straight into the chat. Every message stays in the client’s history with its status.",
  "helpContactRulesTitle": "Contact rules",
  "helpContactRulesBody": "In Colombia, Law 2300 of 2023 applies: collection messages only go out Monday to Friday from 7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. and Saturdays from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., never on Sundays or holidays, always in the debtor’s local time; at most one collection contact per day and a single channel per week. Anything outside the allowed hours is rescheduled automatically to the start of the next valid window, and every decision is recorded with its reason.\n\nTransactional messages (receipt, payoff letter, welcome and statement) also follow the allowed hours by default. The owner can enable immediate sending under Settings › Contact rules: it is a company decision and it is recorded in the audit log.\n\nIf a debtor authorizes other hours in writing, in a document separate from the contract and dated after it, upload it to their documents and record the exception in their profile. The Brazil and USA presets are templates: until your legal counsel reviews them, COROC applies the Colombian one.",
  "helpWhatsappModesTitle": "WhatsApp: assisted and automatic modes",
  "helpWhatsappModesBody": "The WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy forbids using WhatsApp for debt collection and peer-to-peer lending, regardless of licenses. That is why COROC works fully without Meta’s API: assisted mode is on from day one.\n\nAutomatic mode (Cloud API) sends messages on its own, using Meta-approved templates outside the 24-hour window. It can only be turned on with the complete checklist and the owner’s acceptance. If Meta rejects or suspends the account, COROC switches to assisted mode on its own: no message is lost, pending ones wait in “To send today”, and the owner gets a notice by email and in the app.\n\nCOROC never uses unofficial libraries or automates WhatsApp Web: they break WhatsApp’s terms and put the number at risk of a permanent ban.",
  "helpOptOutTitle": "Consent and opt-out",
  "helpOptOutBody": "No message goes out without the debtor’s consent for that channel (WhatsApp or email), recorded with date and method in their profile. The debtor can stop receiving messages at any time: by replying STOP, SALIR or SAIR on WhatsApp, with the button on their portal, or with the unsubscribe link in the email. The opt-out takes effect immediately and blocks anything pending.\n\nIf an email bounces, the address is marked invalid in the client’s profile and is not used again until you fix it. Messages never contain threats, questions about why the debtor has not paid, mentions of third parties, or requests for full card, account or ID numbers: the template validator prevents it.",
