  "desktopResetDone": "Done: the new password works now. Sign in again with it.",
  "desktopResetNoHello": "Changing the password on this PC needs Windows Hello. Turn it on in Windows Settings › Accounts › Sign-in options › PIN and come back here. Another Owner can also set a new password for you.",
  "helpDesktopTitle": "COROC on this PC",
  "helpDesktopBody": "COROC for desktop works inside your PC, with no cloud and no monthly fee. Your data stays on this PC, in your Windows user folder, and only that account can open it.\n\nWhen you close the window, COROC stays next to the Windows clock («COROC keeps working»): it reads email and prepares reminders. To quit completely, right-click the icon and choose «Quit COROC».\n\nTo update, open the new installer: COROC first saves a copy of the database and your data stays intact. In Settings › This PC you can make COROC open by itself when the PC starts.",
  "helpTodayMessagesTitle": "Today's messages via WhatsApp",
  "helpTodayMessagesBody": "COROC prepares the day's reminders, overdue notices, receipts and payoff letters, respecting the allowed hours and limits. In «Today's messages» they appear one at a time: tap «Send» and the client's chat opens in WhatsApp for Windows with the text ready. Press Enter there.\n\nIf the message includes a PDF receipt, COROC copies it for you: in WhatsApp press Ctrl+V and then Enter. When you come back to COROC it moves on to the next one («3 of 12»).\n\nYour WhatsApp number is not connected to any program: you send each message.",
  "helpReceiptsDesktopTitle": "Receiving receipts on the PC",
  "helpReceiptsDesktopBody": "There are three ways, and all of them take the receipt to the Inbox, where COROC reads it and finds the client:\n\n• Drag it from WhatsApp or File Explorer and drop it anywhere in COROC.\n• In WhatsApp right-click the image, choose «Copy», and press Ctrl+V in COROC.\n• If you save it in Downloads, COROC asks «Is it a receipt?».\n\nOnce the payment is recorded, COROC offers to send the receipt via WhatsApp with one click.",
  "helpGmailTitle": "Company Gmail",
  "helpGmailBody": "With the company Gmail connected, COROC checks email every few minutes: if a client sends a receipt, it reads it, records or proposes the payment, replies with the receipt in the same thread and marks the email with the «COROC/Procesado» label. It only reads emails from your clients.\n\nIt connects with a Google «app password» (16 letters), not your Gmail password; if you delete it in Google, COROC stops using the account. Gmail allows about 500 emails a day: COROC uses up to 400 and leaves the rest for the next day. If a client replies STOP, they no longer get emails.",
  "helpDesktopBackupTitle": "Daily backups and changing PCs",
  "helpDesktopBackupBody": "In Settings › Automatic daily backup, choose a folder (OneDrive, Google Drive for desktop or a USB drive) and a password. Every day COROC saves an encrypted .coroc file there and keeps the latest ones. If 7 days go by without a backup, COROC warns you at the top of the screen.\n\nTo move to another PC: install COROC there and, on the first screen, tap «Already used COROC on another PC? Restore a backup». Choose the .coroc file, type the backup password and sign in with your usual username.",
  "helpSmartScreenTitle": "«Windows protected your PC» when installing",
  "helpSmartScreenBody": "Until the COROC installer has a digital signature, Windows may show «Windows protected your PC». This is normal with new programs: click «More info» and then «Run anyway». Only download the installer from the official COROC page."
